# DAC error-counter fix, part 2 of 2 (see dac_fix.md in this directory).
name: dac-fix-2-cave
kind: module
module: 0
region: code
address: 0x03060d8e
gate: build refuses unless the 4 stock bytes at the target equal `expect`;
  the finished image must also pass firmware_patch.validate()
rationale: Reset trampoline in the alignment padding after dac_read.
  0x03060d8e sits in a 14-byte run of `bx lr` filler; an exhaustive scan
  of all 82 modules (BL/B.W targets and literal words) shows zero
  references to 0x03060d8e..0x03060d96. The pad's last two stubs
  (0x03060d98 / 0x03060d9a) ARE referenced as no-op returns by modules
  11 and 61 and are deliberately left byte-identical. Entered only from
  the patched success branch (part 1) with r0 == 0 (successful transfer
  result) and r5 == 0x0300411d (dac_write's counter-block pointer), so
  `strb r0, [r5, #1]` writes 0 to the error counter at 0x0300411e; the
  branch then rejoins the stock tail at 0x03060d1c (movs r0, #0; bus
  release; return transfer result).
expect: 70477047
replace: 6870c4e7
